          "id": "SP_DICEROCARDIUM_CURIONII_STOPPANI_1865",
          "name": "Dicerocardium curionii Stoppani, 1865",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Dicerocardium",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Dicerocardium curionii Stoppani, 1860 - 65, T. 51, figs. 1 - 3. Slightly damaged plaster cast of an internal mould of a specimen originally in the Stoppani collection and lost in 1943. MSNM i 28036 a, b - Fig. 6 Dicerocardium curionii Stoppani, 1860 - 65. T. 52. Reconstructions of the left and right valves of the original shell. The interior surface was based on the plaster cast of a specimen in the Stoppani collection illustrated in T. 51, figs. 1 - 3, of which the previously cited cast has survived. The exterior of the shell was based on the original illustrated in T. 51, figs. 4 and 5, of the Curioni Collection, and is considered lost.",
